def PrivacyPolicy():
    return """PRIVACY POLICY

1. Scope and who is responsible

This Privacy Policy explains what personal information this website and its features (the “Site”) collect, why they collect it, who can see it, and what choices you have. It should be read together with the Site’s Terms of Service (the “Terms”). Terms defined in the Terms, including “Site,” “User Content,” “Site operator,” and “developers,” have the same meaning here.

The Site operator, [SITE OPERATOR NAME, e.g. the Dr. G.W. Williams Secondary School Student Council, with the school’s oversight], decides what information is collected and how it is used. The developers build and maintain the Site’s software. Unless a developer separately and expressly agrees otherwise in writing, the developers do not use personal information from the Site for their own purposes.

The Site may be used by students, families, staff, and other members of the school community. Additional notices shown for a particular feature also apply to that feature.

2. Information we collect

We collect only what is needed to run the Site. The categories are:

(a) Account information. When you register or sign in, we collect your email address and a password. Passwords are stored only as a salted hash and are never stored or displayed in readable form. We may also collect [your name / display name, grade, or other profile fields the Site asks for: CONFIRM].

(b) Verification information. To confirm that a user belongs to the school community, the Site uses join codes, onboarding codes, rotating QR codes, and signed tokens. We store the information needed to operate this system, such as the code or token used, when it was created or used, how many times it has been used, and the account it is linked to. [CONFIRM whether student numbers or any other student identifiers are stored.]

(c) Role and permission information. The Site assigns roles (for example, student, club executive, teacher, teacher administrator, administrator) and records approval of those roles, including who approved or requested a role and when.

(d) User Content and activity. This includes content you submit, such as club information, edits, edit requests, and other materials, together with records of who submitted or changed it and when, so that changes can be reviewed and approved.

(e) Technical information. When you use the Site, our servers and hosting providers receive and may log your IP address, browser and device type, the pages or addresses requested, and the date and time of the request. This information is used for security, troubleshooting, and operating the Site.

(f) Authentication data stored in your browser. After you sign in, the Site stores login tokens in your browser so that you stay signed in. [CONFIRM where: cookies or local storage.] These tokens expire automatically, and the Site uses them only for authentication and security. [CONFIRM whether any analytics or advertising cookies are used. If none, keep: “The Site does not use advertising cookies or sell personal information.”]

(g) Information you send us. If you contact the Site operator or submit a report, we keep that message and your contact details.

We do not intentionally collect sensitive information such as health information, precise location, or government identification numbers. Please do not submit this kind of information through the Site.

3. CAPTCHA and bot protection (Cap)

To protect sign-in and registration from automated abuse, the Site uses a CAPTCHA service called Cap. Cap runs as a separate service operated by the Site operator at [cap.rgsscs.org], not by an outside advertising or analytics company. [CONFIRM against Cap’s own documentation before publishing.]

When the Cap widget appears, your browser contacts that service, which receives the technical information described in section 2(e), such as your IP address and browser details, together with the data your browser sends to complete the challenge. The service is used to decide whether a request looks automated, and the short-lived challenge and verification data it creates is kept in the service’s own temporary data store and is not combined with your account profile or used for advertising or tracking across other sites. [CONFIRM how long challenge data, tokens, and logs are retained.]

The Cap widget may be shown only for certain features, depending on the Site’s settings.

4. How we use information

We use personal information to create and manage accounts; to verify that users belong to the school community; to assign and enforce roles and permissions; to display, review, and approve User Content; to protect the Site against abuse, fraud, and unauthorized access; to investigate reports as described in the Terms; to fix problems and maintain the Site; and to comply with the law and school policies.

We do not sell personal information. We do not use it for advertising or for profiling.

5. Consent, authority, and minors

Many users are students under 18. The Site operator collects personal information only where it has the authority to do so under applicable law and school policy, or with the consent of the individual or, where required, a parent or guardian. If you are under 18, please make sure you have the permission required by your school before using the Site. A parent or guardian may contact the Site operator at any time with questions or to ask about their child’s information.

6. Who can see your information

Other users. Information you choose to publish through a feature, such as club details or content shown on public pages, may be visible to other users or to anyone who visits the Site. Information that is not meant to be public, such as your email, password hash, and verification records, is visible only to the Site operator and authorized administrators as needed for their role.

School officials and authorities. As described in the Terms, the Site operator may share concerns or reports with school officials or appropriate authorities, and may disclose information where required by law.

Service providers. We use outside providers to host and deliver the Site. They process information on our behalf and only to provide their service. These currently include: [Cloudflare (network routing, traffic protection, and secure tunnelling)], [the hosting provider or the Site operator’s own server where the Site and its database run: CONFIRM], and [an email provider, if the Site sends email: CONFIRM]. Map features may load map code and tiles from [OpenStreetMap and a content delivery network], which means your browser connects to those services and they may receive your IP address. [CONFIRM the actual list before publishing.]

Developers. Developers may access Site data only where needed to build, maintain, secure, or fix the Site, and are expected to keep it confidential.

7. Retention

We keep personal information only as long as needed for the purposes in this policy or as required by law or school policy. As a general rule, account and verification information is kept while your account is active and is deleted or anonymized within [PERIOD] after the account is closed, or after you leave the school, unless a longer period is required. Server logs are kept for [PERIOD]. Short-lived tokens expire automatically. As the Terms explain, copies may remain for a limited time in routine backups or in material already shared by other users. [CONFIRM all periods.]

8. Security

We use reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect personal information, including hashed passwords, expiring login tokens, role-based access controls, encrypted connections (HTTPS), and restricted administrator access. No system is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security. Protect your login details and report suspected unauthorized use promptly, as the Terms require. If a breach that creates a real risk of significant harm occurs, we will notify affected people and the appropriate authorities as required by law.

9. Your choices and rights

Subject to applicable law, you may ask to access the personal information we hold about you, to correct it if it is wrong, or to have it deleted or your account closed. We may need to confirm your identity first, and we may keep information we are legally or operationally required to keep, such as records of a report or investigation. To make a request, contact the Site operator using the details in section 12. We will respond within a reasonable time and in any event within the period required by law.

10. Location and transfers

The Site operator is in Ontario, Canada. Some service providers listed in section 6, including Cloudflare, may process information on servers outside Ontario or outside Canada, where it may be subject to the laws of that place. [CONFIRM the physical location of the server that stores the Site’s database.]

11. Applicable law

This policy is intended to be read consistently with the privacy laws that apply to the Site operator and the school, which may include Ontario’s Municipal Freedom of Information and Protection of Privacy Act and Canada’s Personal Information Protection and Electronic Documents Act, as well as school board policy. [CONFIRM with the school which laws and board policies apply.] If this policy conflicts with a mandatory legal requirement or school policy, that requirement or policy governs.

12. Changes and contact

We may update this policy by publishing a revised version on the Site with a new “last updated” date. If a change significantly affects how we use personal information, we will make reasonable efforts to notify users before it takes effect.

Questions, access or correction requests, complaints, or privacy concerns should be directed to: [CONTACT EMAIL OR FORM], or to the school through the contact information published on the Site.
"""